1. Role of proxy.ts

proxy.ts runs before your page loads.

Flow:

Browser requests /admin/dashboard
↓
proxy.ts runs first
↓
proxy checks cookie
↓
allow or redirect
↓
then page/layout loads

Think of it like a gate outside the building.

It is useful for:

blocking protected routes quickly
redirecting logged-in user away from login/register
handling Chrome back button issue
adding headers
basic route control

But it should not contain heavy DB logic.





