# Next.js 16 Navigation Notes

## 1. Link Component

Used for normal navigation between pages.

```tsx
import Link from "next/link";

<Link href="/dashboard">
  Dashboard
</Link>
```

### Characteristics

```txt
Client-side navigation
No full page reload
Most commonly used
SEO friendly
Prefetches pages automatically
```

### Use Cases

```txt
Navbar links
Sidebar links
Dashboard links
Menu items
```

---

# 2. router.push()

Used inside Client Components.

```tsx
"use client";

import { useRouter } from "next/navigation";

const router = useRouter();

router.push("/dashboard");
```

### Characteristics

```txt
Adds a new history entry
User can go back
Client-side navigation
```

### Flow

```txt
Login
↓
router.push("/dashboard")
↓
Dashboard
↓
Browser Back
↓
Login
```

### Use Cases

```txt
Navigate after button click
Navigate after API success
Wizard step navigation
```

---

# 3. router.replace()

Used inside Client Components.

```tsx
router.replace("/dashboard");
```

### Characteristics

```txt
Replaces current history entry
Back button won't return to previous page
Client-side navigation
```

### Flow

```txt
Login
↓
router.replace("/dashboard")
↓
Dashboard
```

### Use Cases

```txt
After Login
After Register
After Logout
Auth redirects
```

### Difference Between push() and replace()

router.push()

```txt
Adds history entry
Back button works
```

router.replace()

```txt
Replaces history entry
Back button does not return
```

