# 7. permanentRedirect()

Used inside Server Components and Server Actions.

```tsx
import { permanentRedirect } from "next/navigation";

permanentRedirect("/new-url");
```

### Characteristics

```txt
Returns HTTP 308 Permanent Redirect
Search engines update URL
Browser may cache redirect
```

### Use Cases

```txt
URL changed permanently
SEO migration
Legacy routes
Domain migration
```

### Example

```txt
/old-blog
↓
/blog
```

Use:

```tsx
permanentRedirect("/blog");
```

---

# Difference Between redirect() and permanentRedirect()

redirect()

```txt
Temporary redirect
HTTP 307
SEO does not treat URL as permanently changed
```

Use when:

```txt
Login redirect
Role redirect
Auth redirect
Temporary navigation
```

---

permanentRedirect()

```txt
Permanent redirect
HTTP 308
SEO updates index
Search engines remember new URL
```

Use when:

```txt
Route permanently moved
Old URL should never be used again
SEO migration
```
Real Example

Old Website
https://roleforge.com/dashboard

Company changes architecture:

https://roleforge.com/app/dashboard

You want every old link:

/dashboard

to automatically go to:

/app/dashboard

and you want Google to remember this permanently.

Use:

permanentRedirect("/app/dashboard");
